From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:41:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Fold the Dispatch and Foundation modules into one module
 named Combine

Apple ships Combine as one module, and code written against it says
`import Combine` and nothing else. The three source folders are compiled
together as that one module, so the imports of OpenCombine from the
Dispatch and Foundation folders go, and every qualifier that named the
module (`OpenCombine.Publisher`, `OpenCombine.Subscriber`, ...) names it
as `Combine`.

The OCombine namespaces existed only so that OpenCombine could sit beside
a system Combine that declares the same names on Foundation's types. In
one module named Combine they are a second spelling of Apple's API, so
the declarations move to where Apple's interface puts them:
Optional.Publisher, Result.Publisher, NotificationCenter.Publisher and
NotificationCenter.publisher(for:object:), Timer.TimerPublisher and
Timer.publish, and DispatchQueue, RunLoop and OperationQueue conforming
to Scheduler themselves with their SchedulerTimeType and
SchedulerOptions. The ocombine accessors, the typealiases that pointed
the plain names at the namespaced ones and the `!canImport(Combine)`
guards around them go with the namespaces. Just and Publishers.Sequence
name the publishers at their new place.
